Subject: [PATCH 410/488] Sink detector: the flags as one TileLang kernel

SinkSampler.flags ran about twelve eager torch kernels a step (index,
abs, amax, nan_to_num, gt, any, arange, searchsorted, index, sub, index,
le, and). One kernel, a thread a logits row, gives the same flags and
values bit for bit: NaN reads 0 and +inf the largest float, as
nan_to_num does; a NaN is never above the threshold; dead rows count
request ends as searchsorted does. A new test pins it against the torch
reference with NaN, +-inf, -0 and values at the threshold.
